# Git LFS for large binaries committed as plain blobs.
#
# lora-dourmouse-claude.gguf (~22MB, repo root): fine-tune weights loaded
# only by the local backend (dourmouse/code_backends.py et al.) — never
# served as a static asset. Safe to move to LFS.
*.gguf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# site/downloads/DourmouseSetup-8.9.0.exe (~28MB) is intentionally EXCLUDED
# from LFS tracking here. site/_headers is a Netlify custom-headers file
# (matches "/downloads/*" with Content-Disposition: attachment) and
# site/index.html links straight to "/downloads/DourmouseSetup-8.9.0.exe" —
# strong evidence a Netlify (or similar static-host) deploy pulls this repo's
# site/ directory and serves that file byte-for-byte from the git checkout.
# No netlify.toml/vercel.json enabling LFS smudge on the build was found in
# this repo. Converting it to an LFS pointer without confirming the deploy
# host resolves LFS pointers would silently break the live download button
# (visitors would receive the ~130-byte pointer text file instead of the
# installer). See README.md "Binary assets & Git LFS" for the follow-up.
#
# site/downloads/*.exe filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text   # NOT enabled — see note above
